# A raised-cosine offset: the shorter the bend, the larger the radiation loss.
# Reference: the same propagation stepped independently in NumPy. The pipeline checks that transmission rises with length.
title S-bend shifting a 0.5 um guide by 1 um over 20 um
window width=24 length=40
guide straight x=0 width=0.5 from=0 to=10
guide sbend x0=0 x1=1 width=0.5 from=10 to=30
guide straight x=1 width=0.5 from=30 to=40
launch mode x=0 width=0.5
monitor out z=40 x=1 width=0.5
plane end z=40
expect power out 0.999942229 2e-7
expect total end 0.999999370 2e-7
expect centroid end 0.9994644 2e-6
expect radius end 0.2805361 2e-6
expect neff 2.631211287 2e-8
